Thanks for the quick response!

I wrote a function to generate the data so I can confirm the estimated alpha and beta:

gen_data <- function(alpha, beta, n = 100){
  theta <- -pi / 2 + pi * runif(n)
  x <- alpha + beta * tan(theta)
  return(x)
}

You don't need to specify the uniform priors for alpha and beta? In this case does the intercept represent alpha? How would you also estimate beta in this context? I'm sorry if these questions are very basic, I'm pretty new to this.

